# Net .wasm budgets for tools/size-check.sh (bytes after wasm-opt -Oz, minus the std runtime).
# Owner guideline: about 100 KB is a real size; raise a budget deliberately, in its own commit,
# when a stage adds a feature that needs it (CLDR data in M5/M6 is measured for 3 locales).
# M4: the probe uses Text, t!, tc! and scope().run; full also carries the CLDR data of M5/M6.
# M6: full formats dates (td, td_as, tdr, Text with {date}): +60 KB for 3 locales (date data
# ~25 KB, the date code with the zones of `tz` and its js-sys glue ~35 KB); 201 KB without them.
MICRO_BUDGET=130000
FULL_BUDGET=270000
# M9: guest is a minimal Rust front end on the Tauri plugin (micro + tauri-guest + global):
# 187 KB measured, the guest's JS glue (js-sys futures, closures) and its parse/apply path.
GUEST_BUDGET=195000
